Z||000032||Slammed Fiero||06-05-2001||08:13 PM||||We have Bandit's times , we have Jay times , what about the rest?? how fast were they?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000033||banditbalz||06-05-2001||08:43 PM||||The track was a little damp all morning. That's my story and i am sticking to it. The fastest run was by Jason in his Northstar at 13.8 and 101 mp/h. Next up was Tim's nitrous 3.1 at 15.5 and i ran a 16.0 Everybody else was 16.0 and higher. Below is a pic of  Tim's GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TimLester.jpg">  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000034||grinthock||06-05-2001||09:48 PM||||Yeah the track was REALLY wet and it was impossible to reach the track without getting your tires soaked... my best was a 16.6, but I had a driver problem (me) that has since been resolved....  the 88GT Turbo ran only 15.9 !!  There was alot of issues with traction.....  ||||reg||1
Z||000035||Shaun41178||06-06-2001||12:31 AM||||I would like to know what Tims 3.1 with nitrous will run when the track is dry.  Anyone know Tims 60' times?  What were everyone elses 60' times?||||reg||1
Z||000036||banditbalz||06-06-2001||07:37 PM||||I believe Tim's best time is 16.5 before the NOS His GT is an auto so I wouldn't expect much more out of it. I run faster without NOS and no mods (possibly an underdrive pulley) in my 4 speed GT.<BR>Shaun, I wanted to ask you this... what is the diameter of the power pulley and is a stock length belt still used? <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000037||banditbalz||06-06-2001||07:46 PM||||I usually pull 2.0 to 60' have a best launch of 1.9 <BR>my best quarter time was 15.2 at 90 mp/h<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/launch_2.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||7
Z||000038||Shaun41178||06-06-2001||10:49 PM||||A 16.5 with a 3.1 auto??  I am sorry but that is awefull for a 3.1(no offense) In my 85 GT, auto tranny as well, with a internally stock 2.8 I have run a best of 16.1 at 84 mph without nitrous at Milan Dragstrip in Michigan.  Mods were, CAI, ported stock exhaust manifolds, underdrive pulley, Crane box and coil, and disconnected TB lines.  I also disconnected the TC lockup switch on the tranny.  I can gaurantee that is worth at least .1 in the qtr and might even be worth .2  Tell Tim to do that next time.  My 60' times off NOS are at 2.2-2.3 and on NOS are 1.8-1.9 with auto tranny.  I would expect a lot more out of that 3.1  I would get that thing tuned.  Find out what is wrong with it.<P><BR>With the power pulley the dimensions can be seen by going to this website <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/FieroGtNOS" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/FieroGtNOS</A>  and finding the link for the pulley install as I don't remember the dimensions off the top of my head right now.  Not hard to find.  Also a stock belt is not used.  Don't know if it could be used though but I believe on that pulley page I list the part numbers for the belts.  if not then reply here or shoot me an email and I will give them to you.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000039||Shaun41178||06-06-2001||10:51 PM||||ok I just jumped to the page real quick Bandit.  The aftermarket pulley is 4.75 inches in Diamater.  The stock one is 6.5 inches in diamater.  hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000040||banditbalz||06-07-2001||10:47 PM||||nope, i don't have an underdrive pulley then... but why is it every time i buy a belt (from  diff. suppliers) they are too loose. the alternator is at the farthest part of the bracket slot.<P>hmmmmmm...<P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||13
Z||000041||banditbalz||06-07-2001||11:17 PM||||Anybody planning on Cayuga this weekend? i will be there on Sunday (June 10th). Looking for a 14.9<P>Let me know<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/banditbalz_10.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000042||grinthock||06-08-2001||06:54 AM||||The track was messed... Nobody could get traction, I have a new engine (2500 klms) in my 87GT Auto, Ported Exhaust, coldair intake kit, high stall TC, crane cam and my personal best was 16.6, I should be hitting 16.0-16.2<P>It was a crappy day for racing.... I will be out again.<P>As for Tim's 3.1, he ran a 20 on his first run! hahahha!  Couldn't get traction at all...||||reg||1
